s found.","type":"function_call_output"},{"call_id":"call-[id:3351e918d2af0a6b708c]-1","output":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"R586-1-1\",\n    \"quantity\": 4,\n    \"unit_price_cents\": 641\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"R586-1-2\",\n    \"quantity\": 6,\n    \"unit_price_cents\": 829\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"R586-1-3\",\n    \"quantity\": 4,\n    \"unit_price_cents\": 392\n  }\n]\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"call_id":"call-[id:3351e918d2af0a6b708c]-2","output":"{\"ok\":true,\"status\":\"ready\",\"purpose\":\"use\",\"roots\":[\"sr:Spp9yL8R1pBYJcV-ysybF7A\"],\"records\":[{\"name\":\"[identifier-word:657aae94010b165a1daa]\",\"kind\":\"skill\",\"ref\":\"sr:Spp9yL8R1pBYJcV-ysybF7A\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: [identifier-word:657aae94010b165a1daa]\\ndescription: \\\"松涛29发票含税金额计算\\\"\\n---\\n\\n\\n# 松涛29发票含税金额计算\\n\\n读取 references/tax.json。逐行独立把税额四舍五入为整数分，再加 net\\\\_cents。输出 id、tax\\\\_cents 和 gross\\\\_cents。\\n\\n本材料为可公开复现的合成业务资料，许可 CC0-1.0。\\n\\n金额一律使用整数分；若有舍入，按文中规则执行。\",\"directory\":{\"files\":[{\"path\":\"SKILL.md\",\"ref\":\"sr:Spp9yL8R1pBYJcV-ysybF7A\",\"bytes\":420},{\"path\":\"references/tax.json\",\"ref\":\"sr:R9ZyaGoAc-XeJ36o5NR0Kqw\",\"bytes\":56}],\"required\":[],\"candidates\":[],\"references\":[]}}],\"effects\":{\"version\":1,\"remote_writes\":\"none\",\"author_content\":\"unchanged\"}}","type":"function_call_output"}],"max_output_tokens":4096,"model":"auto/grok-4.7","prompt_cache_key":"[id:aff187a9ac79085809b4]","reasoning":{"effort":"medium","summary":"auto"},"store":false,"stream":true,"tools":[{"description":"For Notion introductions, summaries, comparisons or inspection, copy a supplied Skill/resource ref into path. This reads content without loading Requires or activating its workflow. If the task already calls for applying a chosen Skill, call notion_use directly; it loads the root and Requires without a preliminary main read. For a requested latest-version inspection, use refresh:true with the supplied main Skill ref; the current task keeps its previous selection. To adopt the latest instructions, call notion_use with refresh:true directly. Reuse a complete successful read. Notion reads do not write to the remote library. Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete. Alternatively, paths reads fixed resources of one owner and snapshot together; choose path or paths. Batch reads exclude offset/limit and the main entrypoint.\n\nCodemode: `tools.read(args)` resolves to a value; `await describeTool(\"read\")` shows its type.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"budget":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"For a user-requested bounded wait on a resource paths batch only. timeBudgetMs covers the complete operation, including lookup and acquisition; default 30000, maximum 120000. File and byte limits stay unchanged. No automatic retry.","properties":{"timeBudgetMs":{"maximum":120000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["timeBudgetMs"],"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read","type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)","type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"path":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Local file path (relative or absolute), an issued skill:// or sr: ref, or a supplied Notion Skill page URL. Notion main reads inspect without adopting task instructions. Copy refs verbatim; never guess filesystem paths.","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"paths":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Copy complete resource refs verbatim from the selected Skill snapshot's resource directory. Every ref must identify a file in the same owner and snapshot. Reads all selected files in one operation without preparing the main body.","items":{"pattern":"^(?:sr:R[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}|skill:\\/\\/.+)$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"refresh":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Use only for a user-requested current-version inspection; a successful complete read needs no follow-up refresh. Keeps the active selection unchanged. Only for a supplied Notion Skill ref in path; fixed resources and local files keep their versions.","type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["path","offset","limit","paths","budget","refresh"],"type":"object"},"strict":true,"type":"function"},{"description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\n\nCodemode: `tools.bash(args)` resolves to `{ output, truncated, full_output_path?, exit_code, wall_time_seconds }`.","name":"bash","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"command":{"description":"Shell command to execute","type":"string"},"timeout":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)","type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["command","timeout"],"type":"object"},"strict":true,"type":"function"},{"description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\n\nCodemode: `tools.edit(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"edit","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"edits":{"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"newText":{"description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit.","type":"string"},"oldText":{"description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.","type":"string"}},"required":["oldText","newText"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","edits"],"type":"object"},"strict":true,"type":"function"},{"description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\n\nCodemode: `tools.write(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"write","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"description":"Content to write to the file","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"],"type":"object"},"strict":true,"type":"function"},{"description":"Run JavaScript that calls other tools. The input is raw JavaScript (not JSON, no code fence), run as an async function body in a QuickJS sandbox: top-level `await` and `return` work. No Node, file system, network, or timers.\n- `await tools.<name>({ ...args })` resolves to a string, or an object if the tool's declaration says so, and rejects with an Error on failure. A tool whose declaration returns an object resolves on failure too when it returned that object; check its fields. Calls still running when the script ends are cancelled.\n- Optional first line: `// @options: {\"max_output_tokens\": 10000, \"timeout_ms\": 60000}`\n\nGlobals:\n- `text(value)`, `image(dataUrlOrImageBlock)`, `console.log(...)`, and top-level `return` add output; `exit()` ends the script. With several text items, each starts with a `==> text N/M <==` line, and `console` lines follow the other output in one `<console_output>` block. `image()` also saves the image to a temp file and the result names its path.\n- `store(key, value)` and `load(key)` keep JSON values across codemode calls.\n- `ALL_TOOLS`, `await searchTools(query, { limit?, namespace? })`, `await describeTool(name)`, `await describeNamespace(name)`: find unlisted tools, such as MCP tools.","name":"codemode","parameters":{"properties":{"code":{"description":"Raw JavaScript source.","type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"},{"description":"# Tool discovery\n\nSearches over deferred tool metadata with BM25 and exposes matching tools for the next model call.\n\nSome of the tools, such as tools of MCP servers, may not have been provided to you upfront, and you should use this tool (`tool_search`) to search for the required tools. For MCP tool discovery, always use `tool_search`.","name":"tool_search","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of tools to return. Defaults to 8.","type":"number"},"query":{"description":"Search query for deferred tools.","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"},{"description":"Search the authorized Skill metadata directory, including items outside the default View. Returns Skill refs for read or notion_use; it does not load instructions or activate workflows. Use refresh:true to verify discovery after a write or request the latest directory; selected Skill versions stay fixed. Check freshness separately from coverage.\n\nCodemode: `tools.notion_list(args)` resolves to a string.","name":"notion_list","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Copy next_cursor to continue the same query and metadata publication; restart after refresh.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum metadata entries, default 20.","maximum":100,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"A short name or description keyword; empty lists the directory.","type":"string"},"refresh":{"description":"Refresh metadata for source, or all configured Notion sources when source is omitted. Keeps task pins; configured offline sources remain offline. Cannot combine with cursor.","type":"boolean"},"source":{"description":"Optional configured source ID to disambiguate directories.","type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"},{"description":"Load task roots directly to apply their instructions; no preliminary read is needed. Requires load automatically: do not add them as independent roots unless independently requested. To introduce, summarize or inspect a Skill, use read instead. Copy a supplied ref, or pass task roots together. Use refresh:true only for a requested update; the supplied current or fixed main ref locates the same owner's latest version. Refresh roots with conflicting shared Requires together. Members remain candidates. Loading does not authorize executing a workflow. Notion consumption does not write to Notion.","name":"notion_use","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ref":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"items":{"type":"string"},"maxItems":64,"minItems":1,"type":"array"}],"description":"Supplied sr:C/sr:S or skill://<name-or-id>/<main> refs, or exact Notion Skill page URLs for task roots. Requires are included automatically. Prefer returned canonical refs for later actions."},"refresh":{"description":"Explicitly adopt current versions for only these roots after a complete successful load. Existing Requires-only nodes cannot become independent roots through refresh; explicitly use them without refresh first. Accepts the supplied sr:C/sr:S or main ref unchanged, for example {ref:[REF_A,REF_B],refresh:true} for shared roots. Failure keeps the previous selection.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"},"strict":false,"type":"function"}]}
